# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Secrets first: an image layer is public to anyone who can pull it, and
# `COPY . .` would bake the .env straight into one. The containers read their
# configuration at run time instead, from the env file compose points them at.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output. Both are produced inside the image; copying the host's would
# ship whatever happened to be lying around, including a Next build made with a
# different NEXT_PUBLIC_GAME_SERVER_URL baked into it.
.next
.game-build
out
dist

node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local tooling and scratch space.
.claude
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Nothing here changes what the server does.
README.md
docker/README.md
*.md
!package.json

# Test and type artefacts.
coverage
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
